But I am in Portugal and my dad has to register this temporary plate, what do I need to bring beside the car and the plates?

===

Since your father is handling the digital registration from Spain while you are driving the car from Portugal, your roles are strictly split (p. 1). 
You are the courier delivering the car and the original paperwork to the physical Spanish import inspection lane (ITV) (pp. 1, 4).To successfully
complete the import inspection in Badajoz without your dad physically present, you must put together a folder containing the following documents:

1. Official Vehicle Documents (Originals Only)The Dutch Registration Documents: Bring the original Dutch vehicle registration certificate (Kentekenbewijs
parts 1 and 2) (p. 1). Photocopies are strictly rejected by the ITV inspector.Certificate of Conformity (CoC): Also known as the Certificado de 
Conformidad. This European standard document details your car's technical specs and emissions data. If you do not have it, you must buy a "Ficha Reducida" 
(a simplified technical sheet) online from an authorized Spanish engineer.

2. Proof of Ownership TransferThe Signed Sales Contract: Bring the handwritten 
or printed Dutch/Spanish purchase agreement between you (or the previous owner) and your father (p. 1). This proves your dad is legally entitled to import
the vehicle under his name (p. 1).

3. Digitally Issued Temporary DocumentsDGT Green Plate Approval: A printed copy of the temporary registration document
(Permiso de Circulación Temporal) that your father downloads after paying the €20.61 fee (p. 1). You will also need this printout to get your green plates 
pressed at the El Nevero shop (pp. 1, 4).Temporary Spanish Insurance (WA): A printed copy of the active green plate insurance policy (e.g., from
Seguropordias.com) (p. 1). The ITV lane will verify that the chassis number matches the policy before they run the tests (p. 1).

4. Identification 
DocumentsYour Father’s Identification: A printed photocopy of his Spanish NIE certificate and his passport/DNI (p. 1).Your Valid Driver's License:
To prove you are legally permitted to drive the vehicle away from the inspection lane once the green plates are mounted (p. 1).
